25,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"It seems we are losing key people and the crews don't always follow the training. We need a vendor that provides heavy, on-site support.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Kenji,,The yards are a mess of old gear and we can't stop for a cutover in winter. We need something rugged and flexible.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The board prefers operating expenses over capital, but bundled pricing is the only thing that has stayed stable over time.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Last winter was a disaster because no one owned the outage. Also, our warehouse rules change too fast for a frozen scope.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,Our internal upgrades are lagging and external data migrations have left us with errors for years. We need reliability.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, does that mean we should avoid external partners for the migration?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Yumi, if the rules change that fast, can any of these vendors actually keep up?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, the lack of ownership you mentioned sounds like a hidden cost in time and productivity.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"Exactly, Toshio. @Kenji, I think we need a system that allows for configuration changes without a total project restart.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, yes, external lifts are risky. We need a vendor that stays until the system actually works.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Misaki,,I agree. A vendor with an engineering team present through the rollout would solve my concerns about the supervisors.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"If we can't have a freeze window, we need a deployment that doesn't break the depot's flow.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Toshio,,I will favor a hosted suite or a bundled agreement to avoid those creeping individual license costs.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Yumi,,I want a single point of contact for support. No more pointing fingers during an outage.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,I'm leaning away from anything that requires us to handle complex upgrades on our own racks if we can't find the staff.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
